title: Proposition 25
---
order: 25
---
short_label: I.25
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two triangles have two sides equal to two sides respectively, but have the base greater than the base, then they also have the one of the angles contained by the equal straight lines greater than the other.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} and {DEF} be two triangles having two sides {AB} and {AC} equal to two sides {DE} and {DF} respectively, namely {AB} to {DE}, and {AC} to {DF}, and let the base {BC} be greater than the base {EF}.

